 "hook": "Here's my leg day as a functional lifter who doesn't squat. Starting with reverse",
 "transcript_start": "Here's my leg day as a functional lifter who doesn't squat. Starting with reverse barbell lunges, I do a warm-up set with 135 and 225. If no one else is around, I like to take my shoes off for extra grip before my top set. I got 315 for 14 reps. Once I hit 20, I usually go up by 5 lb. The reason I don't squat is because I have very deep hip sockets, which also make this movement super secure. If I have the room, I like to do walking barbell lunge",
